cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "quickthink: local-first inference control layer for small LLMs"
abstract: >-
  quickthink is a local-first inference control layer that aims to give small,
  on-device language models more reliable structured output by inserting a
  compressed plan-then-answer scaffold with latency-aware routing. Its routing,
  plan-grammar, and validation logic run as plain-Python middleware (no extra
  model of its own) in front of Ollama-backed calls, with three execution modes
  (lite, two_pass, direct), preset routing profiles, a strict plan grammar, and
  a canonical run/judge/validate/report eval harness.
type: software
